The dataset investigation checklist
A reusable workflow — not every step is mandatory for every dataset.
Progress

0/20



1. Understand provenance
[x] Find the source, README and data dictionary
[x] Identify what one row represents
[x] Understand how and when records were collected


2. Inspect structure
[x] Check shape, columns and dtypes
[x] Inspect head, tail and random samples
[x] Identify numerical, categorical, text and date columns


3. Explore distributions
[x] Use describe for numerical columns
[x] Use value_counts for categorical columns
[ ] Inspect text lengths and date ranges where relevant
[ ] Visualise useful distributions


4. Investigate relationships
[ ] Ask meaningful questions between columns
[ ] Use groupby, crosstab and pivot_table
[ ] Explore correlations and conditional proportions


5. Audit data quality
[ ] Check missing values and duplicates
[ ] Investigate invalid values and outliers
[ ] Verify labels, provenance and possible leakage


6. Decide what to do
[ ] Define the actual problem
[ ] Choose relevant features and target
[ ] Choose a suitable evaluation and splitting strategy
[ ] Establish a simple baseline
